Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:23:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(mobile/system-pip): give way to another device of
 ours with its camera on

The window is for the device the person is using. When the same person is
also in the call on another device (their computer, say) with its camera on,
the window stays closed here, and closes if it's showing; once that device
turns its camera off or leaves, the window may open again (the next time the
app goes to the background). Our camera then goes off in the background as
usual, since the other device is the one being watched.

The same person is the same id in the ticket (the JWT's context.user.id,
which the app gives each person per room, the same on all their devices),
seen in each participant's presence (Prosody's presence_identity puts it
there, so it can't be faked). A main device never gives way to one whose
ticket says device: 'second' (a second-device link, such as a phone over the
desk); a second device gives way to either. Above both, a device the person
explicitly made their main one has context.user.primarySince in its ticket
(seconds): it never gives way to a device of theirs with no such claim or an
older one, so the latest switch wins (and that other device, if it is the
app, gives way to it). Our other devices, and what they share, are never the
one the window shows. Without identities in presence
nobody is matched and the window works as before.
